{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Jethro rejoiced.</b> A form of joy, as in 'תחדהו בשמחה' in Psalms; it is of the same binyan-pattern as 'וישב' from 'שבי,' 'ויפת' from 'בסתר לבי.' Here Rashi explained that people say: a convert is [detested] for ten generations, etc., and they supported this from the verse: 'גם דור עשירי לא יבא להם בקהל ה׳.' And one may say: Ishmael son of Nethaniah, who was of the tenth generation from an Egyptian convert, and he took their vengeance against Israel." "<b>Whom He delivered from the hand of Egypt.</b> For they were still liable to be enslaved, by the decree of 'between the pieces.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:30.384500352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}